{"id":"stage1-child-care","title":"CalWORKs Stage 1 child care in San Francisco, month by month","question":"How many San Francisco children does the county's first-stage welfare-to-work child care pay for, in what kind of care, and at what cost?","finding":"San Francisco reported an average of 667 children a month in Stage 1 child care in 2018-19 and 978 in 2026-27 (989 in 2026-08). In 2026-08, 67% were in license-exempt care (the report's third setting, beside centres and family child-care homes), against 56% statewide. Reimbursed spending is reported through 2023-11 and is zero from 2023-12 on, as is the statewide row; in 2022-23 it averaged $1,060 a child a month ($813 in license-exempt care, $1,240 in centres).","how":"State CW 115 (all CalWORKs families) and CW 115A (two-parent families) monthly reports, San Francisco row of each month, fiscal 2018-19 to the latest month on file. Averages are over months with a figure; masked small numbers ('*') are left out. Spending per child-month is reimbursed spending (item 4) over children with care (item 2) in months that report spending.","limits":"License-exempt care is a setting the report counts beside centres and homes; a high share is not by itself a sign of misuse, and none of these files shows a provider. The zeros from early 2024 look like a change in the form or in what the State publishes, not a stop in payments: the source looks wrong rather than the conduct.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"form","t":"Report","type":"text"},{"k":"year","t":"Year","type":"text"},{"k":"months","t":"Months","type":"int"},{"k":"families","t":"Families a month","type":"int"},{"k":"children","t":"Children a month","type":"int"},{"k":"exemptShare","t":"In license-exempt care","type":"pct"},{"k":"centreShare","t":"In centres","type":"pct"},{"k":"monthsWithSpending","t":"Months reporting spending","type":"int"},{"k":"spentPerChildMonth","t":"Spent per child-month","type":"usd"},{"k":"exemptPerChildMonth","t":"License-exempt, per 